{"id": "EUVD-2026-93118", "enisaUuid": "b4f9a7b5-cdc8-3363-ac4e-d0b31926b1a1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: wilc1000: fix out-of-bounds read in P2P public action frames\n\nwilc_wfi_p2p_rx() and mgmt_tx() start parsing a frame once\nieee80211_is_public_action() returns true. That helper only verifies the\nframe is long enough for the action category field, that is\noffsetofend(struct ieee80211_mgmt, u.action.category), 25 bytes. Both\nfunctions then read the P2P public action header up to oui_subtype at\noffset 30 and pass \"size - ie_offset\" to cfg80211_find_vendor_ie(), where\nie_offset is offsetof(struct ieee80211_mgmt, u) + sizeof(*d), i.e. 32.\n\nA public action frame of 25 to 31 bytes passes the check but is shorter\nthan that 32 byte header, so oui_subtype can be read out of bounds, and\nbecause the length is unsigned, \"size - ie_offset\" underflows to a value\nclose to 4 GiB. cfg80211_find_vendor_ie() takes an unsigned int length,\nso even the size_t subtraction in mgmt_tx() is truncated to the same\nvalue. It then walks far past the buffer searching for a vendor element\nuntil it reaches unmapped memory.\n\nIn the receive path the frame arrives over the air and needs no\nassociation, so a nearby unauthenticated device can crash the host while\nit is in P2P listen. Reject frames shorter than the P2P public action\nheader in both paths before dereferencing it.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:21", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e98ad9f4c59f2e836f8d971b57763a4277680422", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f0c46f8111a479b97b8ab17747c528cade6257f1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a5b827dad8a3037cef04d0240d1c2acb1557101e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/491df93b10d76aebaf6aa4bb05a6ba897f4fccfb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc2ee642ebeac8699b671ddb6d5955a785e5ff43", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/68b786691ce24c5c94e28811db243e573c50f9c1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6fbe76eb2796d2aee45cc6a2dd16e85d3cc96304", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ba6cb7c0868a412c2eb68e8efd5aa38bfb258a14"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98190", "GHSA-hpwv-qhmc-p3v4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "120c90c0-b9a1-3ff7-8964-9e351de43090", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4fb8b5aa2a1126783ae00bae544d6f3c519408ef <cc2ee642ebeac8699b671ddb6d5955a785e5ff43"}, {"id": "17121713-188a-3843-bbf4-c0cc1c11a190", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4fb8b5aa2a1126783ae00bae544d6f3c519408ef <ba6cb7c0868a412c2eb68e8efd5aa38bfb258a14"}, {"id": "17423407-678f-34aa-a135-ec62236aae3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "17a90239-fe36-30ae-920b-0cb431ff1cf6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4fb8b5aa2a1126783ae00bae544d6f3c519408ef <68b786691ce24c5c94e28811db243e573c50f9c1"}, {"id": "19055991-27a9-39d3-9c52-897098728efa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "41dd68c2-95aa-37dd-9fe6-82a76b95189e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "432a7747-1884-3ae3-9ac2-eb84e3ea028d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4fb8b5aa2a1126783ae00bae544d6f3c519408ef <a5b827dad8a3037cef04d0240d1c2acb1557101e"}, {"id": "57d56208-d9a4-399c-9831-7f0f79f243e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4fb8b5aa2a1126783ae00bae544d6f3c519408ef <6fbe76eb2796d2aee45cc6a2dd16e85d3cc96304"}, {"id": "5ca28ee3-6d60-30ad-973c-4d09662a67ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "6738e3d3-1cc5-3995-beff-3f402851cbc4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "68f872ae-610e-3072-a15b-c2c0b59d30c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4fb8b5aa2a1126783ae00bae544d6f3c519408ef <f0c46f8111a479b97b8ab17747c528cade6257f1"}, {"id": "6d7ec2c3-eb67-35a9-9698-7e2507be6ce2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4fb8b5aa2a1126783ae00bae544d6f3c519408ef <491df93b10d76aebaf6aa4bb05a6ba897f4fccfb"}, {"id": "75cd78b6-64b1-38db-9a5b-0346d15dc787", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "8b0d0e14-53b0-3500-93e8-7523a6d09f2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4fb8b5aa2a1126783ae00bae544d6f3c519408ef <e98ad9f4c59f2e836f8d971b57763a4277680422"}, {"id": "912f7d7a-963e-317b-a7a0-82548eb2c351", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "9cfa39e8-7dfb-344d-af36-bf3f6219a1bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "df8a2e7d-44ae-3be7-8971-d740a2f0584c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.7"}, {"id": "eb113f10-bd18-3d8c-9d04-c30ec0bdaa12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1ccecc66-9ddc-33d1-81dc-39c21a9d1b10", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}